  "authored_route_independent_audit": {
    "status": "sufficient-mathematical-preproof-route-only",
    "source_attribution": "Literal SLT final theorem uses Han + signed two-point conditional entropy. Root RMS direct induction is an authored alternative; no claim that SPHMC/SLT prints that route.",
    "chain_identity": "For h on n+1 cube, A=(hT²+hF²)/2=g², Ent_{n+1}(h²)=E_n[(hT²loghT²+hF²loghF²)/2-AlogA]+Ent_n(g²). Same actual finite-law totalmass gives exact cancellation.",
    "RMS_norm": "g=||(hT,hF)||_Euclidean2/sqrt2. Reverse norm contraction gives (g-gprime)²≤((hT-hTprime)²+(hF-hFprime)²)/2, all signed/zero values. Ordinary max-product norm would not justify this exact averaging.",
    "induction_constant": "Conditional twoPoint term gets1/2; IH on g plus RMS contraction and actual Boolean average recovers firstn coordinate energies; last flip swaps slices, its square agrees on both. Total coefficient remains1/2.",
    "cases": "n0 entropy of constant square on unit mass=0, emptyD=0. Bothzero0; onezero entropy(a²/2)log2≤a²/2; mixedsign reverseabs handles squareroots. No division by h/conditionalmean or positive-endpoint premise.",
    "missing_to_be_proved": "Scalar port and all actual finite-law/chain/RMS/induction proofs remain prospective; preproof route approval is not proof completion. Full Han is a sufficient alternative but not mandatory for this endpoint."
